# M8's done-when on QEMU with the selftest kernel (user/root/src/tui.rs;
# docs/design.md, "Scenarios" under "Framebuffer, terminal and TUI"): a
# TUI app runs inside a terminal emulator that draws to the framebuffer,
# and the screendumps of it match the host render. The root task starts
# watch, uart and console, attaches as client 1 and prints through
# console; checks the framebuffer (the std VGA, pinned at 1280x800 below
# so the goldens' size does not rest on QEMU's default) and prints its
# frame plan; times a full clear mapped uncached, then write-combining
# [H10] (TCG has no cache model, so the times mean nothing here); starts
# term (125), with the framebuffer mapped write-combining in its VSpace
# alone, and tui (100); shows each framebuffer frame it holds mapped (a
# second Frame_Map refused as mapped, a Frame_Remap without read refused
# for its rights), prints the priorities it set with the MCPs it reads
# back; then waits on endpoint D. tui asks term's Size,
# writes its banner, enters the alternate buffer and draws its first
# frame. Keys typed for console's raw client 4 (Ctrl-T 4 focuses it)
# reach term through ReadRaw and tui through term's Read: Down, Down,
# Enter opens the Colours panel; q quits, back to the main buffer with
# the banner and the goodbye. Root checks tui read exactly the 8 bytes
# typed for it, and term's Stats: nothing ignored, nothing dropped. Each
# screendump follows a line printed only after term answered the frame's
# last Write, and is taken while every thread that could draw is blocked:
# the screen holds still until the send: after it. The goldens come from
# the host render (xtask's tui_screendumps_are_the_host_render), never
# from QEMU.
cmdline: test=tui
exit: success
qemu_args: -vga std -global VGA.xres=1280 -global VGA.yres=800
expect: root: cmdline "test=tui"
expect: fb: 1280x800 BGR, stride 1280, 4000 KiB at 0x80000000: 6 untyped, 1 2 MiB and 488 4 KiB frames; 160x50 cells
expect: fb: full clear: uncached
expect: servers: term and tui started; root CNode
expect: fb: all 489 frames are mapped: a second Frame_Map of each is refused as mapped, and a Frame_Remap without read for its rights
expect: servers: priority as set, MCP as read back: console 150, 150; term 125, 125; tui 100, 100
expect: tui: 160x50 terminal
expect: tui: frame 1 drawn: Overview, item 1
screendump: tui-main
send: \x144                        # Ctrl-T 4: focus term
expect: [console] focus 4 (term)
send: \e[B\e[B\r                   # Down, Down, Enter
expect: tui: frame 4 drawn: Colours, item 3
screendump: tui-colours
send: q
expect: tui: quit after 4 keys
expect: tui: read 8 bytes: \e[B\e[B\rq
expect: term: stats:
expect: , 0 ignored,
expect: , 0 dropped
expect: root: the TUI has quit; Ctrl-T 1 and Enter end the test
screendump: tui-quit
send: \x141\r                      # Ctrl-T 1, Enter: root's line
expect: [console] focus 1 (root)
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
forbid: TEST FAIL
